[P_03_Bank_Communications]
Speech_0207L=LAMBERT - Fisher, the arms that Lacerda had were purchased by someone using a Panamanian offshore bank as proxy. I want to take a peek inside their records... unfortunately, it's not as simple as that. This op can't look like a US intelligence gig, so to cover it up you'll need to crack the bank's vault and lift some bearer bonds - property of the French Government.
Speech_0208L=GRIMSDOTTIR - I hit the Bank's server's last night, but I didn't find much. All their work stations run drivers for plug and play hard-drives. I'm guessing they secure them physically every night.  Crazy world we live in where electronic intrusion is more of a threat than physical intrusion... Anyway, they probably store the drives in the main vault meaning they're not going to be easy to get a hold of.
Speech_0209L=REDDING - First, the good news. You've been in this bank before. You were part of a CIA raiding team that went in in '89 looking for some of Noriega's drug money. Most of the intelligence we have on the bank actually comes from your team. The bad news is that we have a lot of physical security. Lasers, motion sensors, locked doors, cameras, the whole lot, and none of it was there in '89... We've also contacted a... uh... specialist... to help crack the vault. You better talk to him.
Speech_0210L=TURTLE - Look... I don't know who you are, or why I'm helping you other than that it's better than staring at the ceiling in my cell. I hear you have to face a Mason Wells 88. Well, it ain't a one man job... but they tell me you can do the work of five men. Fine I says. I had your mate Willy make a little deposit for you. You'll be needing some things from a safety box in the little vault that we can use to crack the main one.
Speech_0211L=PARTRIDGE - We'll continue on our course for the Yellow Sea and send you back by helicopter to Panama City. I have no authorization to act inside Panamanian borders, so you'll be operating covertly out of the Embassy. You and your partner will be on your own in Panama.
Speech_0252L=O'DELL - Chinese Ambassador to the United States, Long Dan, was recalled to China today for an emergency meeting with government officials regarding ongoing problems between Korea and Japan. Long Dan is expected to renew his efforts to bring Korean, US and Japanese delegates to the bargaining table.
Speech_0253L=O'DELL - In sports... pitcher Akira Watanabe arrived in New York yesterday for his first practice with his new team. After a full day of evaluations, head pitching coach Mathieu Ferland stated that Watanabe was, quote, easily the best baseball pitcher ever...
POPUPMESSAGE_0265=Alarm Stage One
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0224L=LAMBERT - Fisher... watch the alarms... this is a bank robbery after all.
POPUPMESSAGE_0266=Alarm Stage Two - Enemies Equipping Body Armor
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0225L=LAMBERT - I'm serious Sam... too many alarms and you'll have the whole Panamanian Army after you.
POPUPMESSAGE_0267=Alarm Stage Three - Enemies Equipping Helmets
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0226L=LAMBERT - Fisher... I'm not kidding around. One more alarm and you'll be in big trouble.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0227L=LAMBERT - Dammit, Sam. They called a general alarm... you're going to have to battle your way through now. Complete your primary objectives and get out of there!
Speech_0272L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, I've added some info about the bank to your OPSAT.
Speech_0027L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Fisher, I just synched your OPSAT with intelligence on the bank that you and your team gathered back in '89.
Speech_0028L=FISHER - Ah the memories...
Speech_0029L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Yeah... judging from your report... sounds like it was quite a vacation...
Speech_0030L=FISHER - It was actually. I spent most of the rest of that year sleeping in a ditch on the road between Baghdad and Kuwait.
Speech_0031L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Oh. Well... if it's any consolation, I had a bad year that year too.
Speech_0032L=FISHER - What? You weren't working for the government during the Gulf War...
Speech_0033L=GRIMSDOTTIR - No. I was in Tenth Grade...
Speech_0034L=FISHER - Oh. Right. Yuck.
Speech_0228L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, I've added some info about the bank to your OPSAT.
Speech_0273L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, you'll need to disable a junction box on the roof to switch off the magnetic locks on the rooftop windows.
Speech_0111L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Fisher, I've got a copy of a work order here that the bank filed with their insurance company. It says the dome windows over the lobby are magnetically locked. See if you can find a breaker or junction box up here and power down the locks.
Speech_0114L=FISHER - Right.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0229L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, you'll need to disable a junction box on the roof to switch off the magnetic locks on the rooftop windows.
Speech_0274L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Lasers just came on line in the lobby Sam.
Speech_0115L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Good work Sam, that shut down the magnetic locks on the windows... hey... wait a minute... power spike. The lobby... it looks like a laser grid just came on line...
Note_0254L=Laser sensors are active in the lobby and upstairs hallways.
Speech_0118L=FISHER - Lasers? Lasers are so...
Speech_0119L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Nineties... ?
Speech_0120L=FISHER - I was going to say seventies... can you please stop making me feel old.
Speech_0121L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Got bad news for you Sam... you are old.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0230L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Lasers just came on line in the lobby Sam.
Note_0259L=Laser sensors are active in the lobby and upstairs hallways.
Speech_0275L=TURTLE - I got the serial number. Now you need to tap the authorization locks in the security office, the President's Office and the Treasurer's Office.
Speech_0050L=LAMBERT - Fisher, here's our advisor. He'll walk you through the steps that will get you into that vault... be patient with him...
Speech_0053L=FISHER - Oh... he's one of those...
Speech_0054L=TURTLE - Right! Hello? Is this thing on then?
Speech_0057L=FISHER - It's on. I'm here. Have you been briefed?
Speech_0060L=TURTLE - Whatever. Listen... this is a Mason Wells 88. Each one is unique. You wanna get a peek up this girls skirt, first thing you'll need to do is authorize an opening.
Speech_0256L=FISHER - How do I do that?
Speech_0257L=TURTLE - The Bank President and the Treasurer will each have an authorization lock in their office. There'll be another one in the security office. You'll need to disable all three.
Speech_0258L=FISHER - Ok.
Speech_0061L=FISHER - Where do I find that?
Speech_0062L=TURTLE - Under the main lobby floor, there should be a vent system over the vault. I'm guessing you'll be able to scan the barcode from in there.
Speech_0065L=FISHER - Gotcha.
Speech_0237L=TURTLE - Right... we need to sneak a peak at the vault's serial number. It's etched as a barcode on the vault casing. You'll be able to read it from the vent system under the lobby floor.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0246L=LAMBERT - Don't get ahead of yourself, Fisher. You need to scan the serial number for the vault before you'll have any chance of getting inside it.
Speech_0247L=FISHER - Alright... I'll head back.
Speech_0248L=LAMBERT - Sam, get the serial number for the vault before you proceed.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0066L=TURTLE - There you are... that's yer serial number. 091772 series. That means she's a four step tango. First thing you'll need to do is authorize an opening.
Speech_0071L=FISHER - How do I do that?
Speech_0072L=TURTLE - The Bank President and the Treasurer will each have an authorization lock in their office. There'll be another one in the security office. You'll need to disable all three.
Speech_0073L=FISHER - Ok.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0238L=TURTLE - I got the serial number. Now you need to tap the authorization locks in the security office, the President's Office and the Treasurer's Office.
Note_0260L=Guards patrolling laser grids have beacons that disable the grid locally.
Speech_0276L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Stick close to the patrolling guard and you can avoid the lasers.
Speech_0122L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Looks like more lasers ahead Sam. This whole places is singing with photons...
Speech_0123L=FISHER - There's a guard who seems to be walking around here with no problems...
Speech_0124L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Maybe he has some kind of beacon... get close and you can stay in his electronic shadow...
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0231L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Stick close to the patrolling guard and you can avoid the lasers.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0074L=TURTLE - That's the President's authorization. Two more to go.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0075L=TURTLE - That's the Treasurer's authorization. Two more to go.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0076L=TURTLE - That's the security authorization. Two more to go.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0077L=TURTLE - That's two down. Now just authorize from the President's office.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0078L=TURTLE - That's two down. Now just authorize from the Treasurer's office.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0079L=TURTLE - That's two down. Now just authorize from the security office.
Speech_0277L=TURTLE - Authorization is done. Head to the vault. There is some equipment for you in a safety deposit box.
Speech_0080L=TURTLE - Right... that's authorization done. The outer cage to vault should be opening as we speak.
Speech_0081L=FISHER - Great.
Speech_0083L=TURTLE - Just inside the cage there's a small vault full of safety deposit boxes. You're mate dropped off some kit for you in one of them.
Speech_0084L=FISHER - Alright... I'll let you know when I'm there.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0239L=TURTLE - Authorization is done. Head to the vault. There is some equipment for you in a safety deposit box.
Speech_0278L=REDDING - The gear you need is in safety deposit box 1024.
Speech_0085L=REDDING - Sam, it's Will...
Speech_0086L=FISHER - Turtle said one of these boxes had some equipment in it?
Speech_0087L=REDDING - Chest level, right hand side. Number 1024.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0234L=REDDING - The gear you need is in safety deposit box 1024.
Speech_0279L=TURTLE - Take the new kit and get to the main vault.
Speech_0088L=TURTLE - Careful with that gear.
Speech_0089L=FISHER - What is all this stuff?
Speech_0090L=TURTLE - The charges are for the vault and the other do-hickey is a telemetric lock pick.
Speech_0091L=FISHER - A telemetric lock pick?
Speech_0092L=TURTLE - Head down to the main vault... we'll walk you through it there.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0240L=TURTLE - Take the new kit and get to the main vault.
Speech_0280L=TURTLE - To pick two locks simultaneously you need to use the telemetric pick. Place the male end in one lock and the female in the other. Pick the female end and your movements will be replicated in the male end.
Speech_0095L=TURTLE - Alright, next you need to pop both of these locks at the same time.
Speech_0096L=FISHER - That's what the telemetric pick is for.
Speech_0097L=TURTLE - Exactly, it reads your movements in one lock and mimics them in the other lock, real-time.
Speech_0098L=FISHER - You guys use some cool toys.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0241L=TURTLE - To pick two locks simultaneously you need to use the telemetric pick. Place the male end in one lock and the female in the other. Pick the female end and your movements will be replicated in the male end.
Speech_0281L=TURTLE - Right, now once you got the feel for each pin, you have to wait a second for the telemetric pick to synch up. Once it beeps you can pick the pin and move to the next one. Don't try and pick a pin before you're in synch, or you'll have to restart.
Speech_0249L=TURTLE - Right, now once you got the feel for each pin, you have to wait a second for the telemetric pick to synch up. Once it beeps you can pick the pin and move to the next one. Don't try and pick a pin before you're in synch, or you'll have to restart.
Speech_0250L=FISHER - Right.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0251L=TURTLE - Right, now once you got the feel for each pin, you have to wait a second for the telemetric pick to synch up. Once it beeps you can pick the pin and move to the next one. Don't try and pick a pin before you're in synch, or you'll have to restart.
Speech_0282L=TURTLE - Alright, now place the charges over the main pins and blow 'em.
Speech_0103L=TURTLE - Alright, now place the charges over the main pins. Once they're all in place... well, I'm sure you can figure it out.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0242L=TURTLE - Alright, now place the charges over the main pins and blow 'em.
Speech_0283L=LAMBERT - Great work. Sam, get in there and find those harddrives.
Speech_0106L=TURTLE - And... open sesame...
Speech_0107L=FISHER - Lambert... we're in.
Speech_0108L=LAMBERT - Great work. Sam, get in there and find those harddrives.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0243L=LAMBERT - Great work. Sam, get in there and find those harddrives.
Speech_0284L=LAMBERT - That's the first of the eight mails uploaded, Fisher. Seven to go.
Speech_0002L=LAMBERT - That's a relief. Our installer seems to be compatible with their local OS.
Speech_0003L=FISHER - That's it? Just plug and play...
Speech_0004L=LAMBERT - That's the idea. No fuss. Get all eight of those forged mails uploaded.
Speech_0005L=FISHER - Make the robbery look like an inside job...
Speech_0082L=LAMBERT - Exactly.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0212L=LAMBERT - That's the first of the eight mails uploaded, Fisher. Seven to go.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0006L=LAMBERT - That's half of the forged mails Sam. Four more to go.
Speech_0007L=FISHER - Thanks... I've always found it hard to count past 3...
Speech_0008L=LAMBERT - No need to be smarmy Sam...
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0009L=LAMBERT - Great work Fisher, one more forged mail and we're covered.
Speech_0010L=FISHER - Doin' my best.
Speech_0285L=LAMBERT - Great work Sam, that's all the forged emails.
Speech_0011L=LAMBERT - Great work Fisher. Now any investigation into the robbery will only point back at the investigators...
Speech_0012L=FISHER - So the Panamanian government will end up sending some innocent banker to prison?
Speech_0013L=LAMBERT - Innocent if you don't count providing arms to revolutionaries...
Speech_0014L=FISHER - Oh... right... I forgot... bankers: evil.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0213L=LAMBERT - Great work Sam, that's all the forged emails.
Speech_0286L=LAMBERT - Damn it Fisher. You destroyed one of the computers that we needed to upload a mail to. Consider your opportunity objectives aborted.
Speech_0017L=LAMBERT - Damn... That computer was one of the ones we needed to plant a forged email on.
Speech_0018L=FISHER - Oh... I guess that scraps my opportunity objective?
Speech_0019L=LAMBERT - Unfortunately.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0214L=LAMBERT - Damn it Fisher. You destroyed one of the computers that we needed to upload a mail to. Consider your opportunity objectives aborted.
Speech_0287L=LAMBERT - Good job Fisher, now the whole mission will look like a robbery.
Speech_0023L=LAMBERT - Good job Fisher... now the whole mission will look like a robbery... they'll never know why we were here.
Speech_0024L=FISHER - Lambert... now that I'm holding fifty million bucks... I think we need to talk about that raise again...
Speech_0025L=LAMBERT - Hm... twenty-five cents an hour and not a penny more.
Speech_0026L=FISHER - Deal.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0215L=LAMBERT - Good job Fisher, now the whole mission will look like a robbery.
Speech_0288L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, the emails relating to Lacerda are all purged but some fragments indicate that they came from someone named Dvorak. They were all encrypted using a 512 bit key, which is extremely sophisticated and classified.
Speech_0036L=GRIMSDOTTIR - I have fragments of a message here from someone named 'Dvorak'. Echelon doesn't have a file on him... Wait... that's weird.
Speech_0043L=FISHER - What?
Speech_0044L=GRIMSDOTTIR - The deleted messages. They're five-twelve encrypted... I haven't seen five-twelve since Phillip Masse.
Speech_0045L=FISHER - I killed Masse outside Severomorsk.
Speech_0046L=GRIMSDOTTIR - I remember. And it's confirmed... so this is someone with access to some seriously classified information...
Speech_0047L=FISHER - Who?
Speech_0048L=GRIMSDOTTIR - I'm not sure... I'll get back to you.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0232L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, the emails relating to Lacerda are all purged but some fragments indicate that they came from someone named Dvorak. They were all encrypted using a 512 bit key, which is extremely sophisticated and classified.
Speech_0167L=FISHER - Zherkezhi?
Speech_0168L=GRIMSDOTTIR - That's a frightening possibility.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0233L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, the emails relating to Lacerda are all purged but some fragments indicate that they came from someone named Dvorak. They were all encrypted using a 512 bit key, which is something that Morgenholt and Zherkezhi had access to...
Speech_0289L=REDDING - Sam, you need to complete your primary objectives before we can extract you.
Speech_0205L=REDDING - Sam, you need to complete your primary objectives before we can extract you.
Speech_0206L=FISHER - Gotcha.
