[P_03_Bank_SecurityPostA]

[P_03_Bank_SecurityPostB]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0003L=SOLDIER - So, you know how the other night I was covering Colon's shift right?
Speech_0004L=SOLDIER - Yes...
Speech_0005L=SOLDIER - Well, I'm patrolling past the janitor room and I hear something... I look inside and I hear singing...
Speech_0006L=SOLDIER - Singing? From where?
Speech_0007L=SOLDIER - Well that's the thing... I search the room, but I can't find anything... but I definitely hear singing... and later, I'm over on this side and I hear Rodrigo singing the same song...
Speech_0012L=SOLDIER - So it was Rodrigo in the janitor room?
Speech_0013L=SOLDIER - No... there was no one there. But you know the vent in the janitor room? I think that vent connects to this side... to the men's bathroom... I think that's how I heard Rodrigo...
Speech_0014L=SOLDIER - You mean Rodrigo sings while he's going to the bathroom? Eeuuww.

[P_03_Bank_SRCfirst]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=SOLDIER - Hey... I was just thinking something...
Speech_0002L=SOLDIER - What's that?
Speech_0003L=SOLDIER - Did you ever notice that this bank doesn't have any bank machines?
Speech_0004L=SOLDIER - Of course...
Speech_0005L=SOLDIER - Why do you think that is?
Speech_0006L=SOLDIER - Because they don't want people to hack the bank machines.
Speech_0007L=SOLDIER - Hack a bank machine? Who ever heard of that?!
Speech_0008L=SOLDIER - It's not the realism that's the problem... it's just that it introduces a whole resource economy that we don't want to deal with...
Speech_0009L=SOLDIER - Oh... oh... I see your point.

[P_03_Bank_SRCsecond]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=SOLDIER - Ugh, these uniforms are so uncomfortable.
Speech_0009L=SOLDIER - Oh... that's one of new American made ones.
Speech_0010L=SOLDIER - So that's good... they're not made by second rate laborers bidding to low ball each other on a Panamanian Army service contract.
Speech_0011L=SOLDIER - Oh, make no mistake... the quality of these uinforms is exemplary... they'll never wear out...
Speech_0012L=SOLDIER - So?
Speech_0013L=SOLDIER - Well, they're about five degrees hotter, they weight about eight ounces more, they don't breath at all, and their itchy.
Speech_0014L=SOLDIER - Well it doesn't sound like a very good business move to me... why would the Americans do that?
Speech_0015L=SOLDIER - From a business perspective it's a terrible move... but let me ask you this...
Speech_0016L=SOLDIER - What?
Speech_0017L=SOLDIER - Hypothetically speaking... if you had to invade Panama... would you rather fight an Army with disposable, second rate uniforms, or an army who was overburdened, overheated, itchy and couldn't move well?
Speech_0018L=SOLDIER - Oh... I didn't think of it that way...
Speech_0019L=SOLDIER - No... no... neither did our generals when they pocketed a juicy US contract for ever-lasting uniforms... there are many ways to wage war my friend...

[P_03_Bank_SRCultimate]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=SOLDIER - Did you hear the latest news? The Americans just announced that they have a problem with the rescue shuttle.
Speech_0006L=SOLDIER - What kind of problem?
Speech_0007L=SOLDIER - Some kind of malfunction in one of the rocket assemblies... the parts required will take weeks to manufacture.
Speech_0008L=SOLDIER - I thought they said the astronauts only had a few days of life support...
Speech_0009L=SOLDIER - That's what they said.
Speech_0010L=SOLDIER - So... so what... they're just going to die up there...
Speech_0011L=SOLDIER - That's what it look like...
Speech_0012L=SOLDIER - That's horrible.
Speech_0013L=SOLDIER - I'll say.

